- LEGAL PAGES + MARKETING CONSENT: no privacy policy, terms, or returns policy exists, and nothing can go live without them.
  - Practically mandatory, for three separate reasons: Stripe/PayPal require a published privacy policy in their terms
    and hold accounts at review without one; CalOPPA requires one for any commercial site collecting PII from California
    residents with NO revenue threshold; GDPR Arts. 13-14 require a notice at the point of collection the moment an EU/UK
    shopper signs up. CCPA/CPRA's "Do Not Sell or Share" duty only bites above ~$25M revenue / 100k consumers.
  - Live defect today: register-form.tsx renders "By creating an account, you agree to our Privacy Policy and Terms of
    Use." as PLAIN TEXT. The documents do not exist and the words are not links, so we assert agreement to something
    unreachable. Either write them and link, or drop the sentence — the current state is worse than silence.
  - Footer Help/Company links all point at `/` for the same reason (see components/footer.tsx). Static content routes
    are the shared prerequisite.
  - Marketing consent is a SEPARATE consent from the privacy policy and needs storage we do not have: a
    `customer.acceptsMarketing` column, the field on StoreSignupBody, and the signup route threading it into
    customerData. Under GDPR it must be opt-in and unticked by default — never pre-checked.
  - Selling into the EU also drags in a 14-day right of withdrawal with pre-contractual disclosure, and a cookie banner
    if we ever add non-essential cookies. Get a lawyer to review before taking live payments.
